### 🛡️ About Me

Security Analyst with 2+ years of hands-on SOC experience in alert triage, incident investigation, and log correlation across phishing, authentication, endpoint, and network security incidents. Skilled in using Microsoft Sentinel, Splunk, and Microsoft Defender for Endpoint to investigate and validate security incidents, with strong query-writing ability in KQL and SPL for correlating Windows Event Logs and endpoint telemetry. Experienced in independently handling end-to-end investigations within a lean SOC team, from initial triage through documentation and closure. Also skilled in static and dynamic malware analysis, having analyzed real-world malware families including XWorm, AsyncRAT, and AgentTesla in an isolated lab environment, extracting IOCs and mapping behavior using PEStudio, Procmon, Process Explorer, and ANY.RUN. Beyond core SOC operations, built a SOAR automation workflow in Tines integrating the URLScan.io API for automated URL analysis. Continuously upskilling through hands-on cybersecurity learning platforms and instructor-led workshops, with active learning in progress toward Microsoft SC-200 (Security Operations Analyst).

